  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "1ac581ef-7f20-4197-80fc-156a956d48e9",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -224,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 896,
        "content": "## Self-Healing Job Radar\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow runs on a schedule to scan a list of organisations for current job vacancies. It validates or discovers each organisation\u2019s career page, scrapes the page with Firecrawl, uses OpenAI to extract open roles, removes roles already known in Airtable, and stores only new vacancies. It loops through organisations and then through new roles so the radar can keep itself up to date over repeated runs.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure the Schedule Trigger with the desired scan frequency.\n- Connect Airtable credentials and verify the Organisations table contains organisation records and a career page field such as \"Career Page\".\n- Connect Airtable credentials for the Vacancies table and ensure it has fields required by the workflow for deduplication and storing new roles.\n- Add Firecrawl API credentials or headers to both Firecrawl HTTP Request nodes.\n- Configure the OpenAI node with valid OpenAI credentials and confirm its extraction prompt returns a structured list of roles compatible with the Split Out node.\n- Review the URL field names and Airtable record IDs used by the update and store steps so writes go to the correct base and tables.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the schedule frequency, Firecrawl scrape options, OpenAI extraction prompt, and deduplication criteria to match the target job markets and the fields stored in Airtable."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "510bdbea-6127-4d60-950d-a693756d00a8",
